# Necromancer — one of the Henchmen of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 10/12 The Henchmen — up to 27 life, can't be bribed
# enemy: Necromancer (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0291.dck "Necromancer (Bl, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 15 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 13 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/necromancer.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 10)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/necromancer.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Henchmen) — "Necromancer" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Necromancer
22 Swamp
2 Dark Ritual
4 Evil Presence
2 Unholy Strength
2 Drain Life
4 Scathe Zombies
4 Zombie Master
4 Bog Wraith
2 Wall of Bone
4 Lost Soul
2 Bad Moon
2 Raise Dead
2 Necropolis of Azar
2 Animate Dead
2 Cosmic Horror
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Evil Presence
#   .vBlack  2 Paralyze, 1 Throne of Bone
#   .vBlue   3 Evil Presence
#   .vGreen  3 Evil Presence
#   .vRed    3 Evil Presence
#   .vWhite  3 Evil Presence
SB: 2 Paralyze
SB: 1 Throne of Bone
